      "writtenOn": "2025-10-17T00:08:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems to be quite error-prone and assumes a specific format of the input. I looked into it and it seems like the file format is generally \"Python\", as DEPS files are `exec`\u0027d: https://crsrc.org/c/buildtools/checkdeps/builddeps.py;l\u003d124;drc\u003df4ee964fb1d71dae4c7243ac78c76949c95906e5\n\nWhile I don\u0027t have a super strong opinion - an imperfect formatter is much better than no formatter - have we considered using an AST-based approach instead? For example, could we start off using the existing formatter used for Python files, maybe with a different configuration?",
      "revId": "734f1a6355f92238fcd5626238da6073a5da63da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
